# Rasterising Azgaar's terrain (W2b) with detail (W3a): a hand-made export of five cells
# imported into a map file, then read back. The tile counts and heights were worked out by a
# separate script.

# The whole map at 1 tile a pixel, with the default detail; its length is in the snapshot.
world import crates/content/tests/fixtures/azgaar/raster.json target/raster.map

# What it wrote: the recipe names the export's fingerprint.
world info target/raster.map

assert world import crates/content/tests/fixtures/azgaar/raster.json target/off.map --region 30,30,20,20 == error: the region runs off the source map: pixels (30, 30) to (49, 49), and the map is 40 × 40 pixels
assert world import crates/content/tests/fixtures/azgaar/raster.json target/off.map --region 10,10 == error: --region needs four whole numbers, <x>,<y>,<width>,<height>, not 10,10
assert world import crates/content/tests/fixtures/azgaar/raster.json == error: world needs the form: world info <file>, world source <file>, or world import <export> <map> [--region <x>,<y>,<width>,<height>] [--scale <n>] [--seed <n>] [--detail <strength>] [--wavelength <pixels>] [--octaves <n>]

# Rougher detail, and another seed, in the recipe: heights -381.73 to 2241.02 m, and the
# recipe's detail in what `world info` says. The lengths are in the snapshot.
world import crates/content/tests/fixtures/azgaar/raster.json target/rough.map --seed 3 --detail 0.5 --wavelength 4 --octaves 2
world info target/rough.map
assert world import crates/content/tests/fixtures/azgaar/raster.json target/rough.map --octaves 9 == error: the detail needs 1 to 8 octaves, not 9
